Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:47:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] docs(compact-core): document reserved words and when
 ledger fields need export

Agents in an independent pilot repeatedly wrote `const from = ...` in
transfer circuits (parse error: found keyword "from"). compact-core
documented `function` and `delete` as reserved, but not `from` or the
other keywords. Adds a Reserved Words section verified against compiler
0.36.0, a compilation-review check for keywords used as names, and a
check for ledger fields that off-chain code reads but that lack
`export` (they compile but are missing from the TypeScript Ledger type).

Bumps compact-core to 0.12.1.

Signed-off-by: Z <212753116+xena-z@users.noreply.github.com>
